  "issue_number": 389,
  "issue_title": "Feature: freeze stable architecture and local model/tool/skill/workflow contracts",
  "issue_body": "## Problem\nThe architecture, tool, skill, workflow, and policy contracts have evolved through milestones 1\u201314 but have not been formally frozen and versioned. Without a stable contract surface, the 1.0 release cannot guarantee backward compatibility.\n\n## Proposed behavior\nAudit and freeze all contracts: tool API, skill SKILL.md schema, workflow schema, policy rule format, model manifest, and memory entry schema. Document each contract version with a changelog. Mark any remaining unstable fields as experimental or remove them before 1.0.\n\n## User workflow\n1. Maintainer runs the contract audit checklist.\n2. Each contract is versioned and documented.\n3. Release notes list the frozen contract versions and any breaking changes since M14.\n\n## Local-first impact\nAll frozen contracts ship with the app; version validation is local.\n\n## Safety and security considerations\n- Policy contract freeze must not silently widen permissions.\n- Experimental contracts must be clearly flagged.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n- Continue evolving past 1.0 without freezing: breaks external tool/skill authors.\n- Freeze everything: blocks necessary iteration; experimental marker solves this.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-03T20:41:25.000Z",
